2186045417 true] [17592186430360 1072 #uuid "2cc63714-8ef0-5462-b695-51b69677adfb" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430360 1074 "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{5}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.\n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430361 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430364 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430361 1062 #uuid "6ec7950f-72d8-5bef-a77f-3f5e2a3e06a0" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430361 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162712 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430362 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430363 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430362 1062 #uuid "ac4c51ea-2c80-5f4f-b061-1215e274de99" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430362 1063 #edb/ref 17592186430360 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430363 1062 #uuid "db830862-a12c-5ef8-aeb2-df43d7cd0bdb" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430363 1063 #edb/ref 17592186430359 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430364 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430362 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430364 1062 #uuid "f69ed049-06d6-5162-954f-63ae0c151052" 13194139534634 17592186045417 true] [17592186430364 1063 #edb/ref 17592186371422 13194139534634 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-7a17cc21-6ccb-5439-ab56-b058df3482c5" 17592186430259 "answer-08e2fd28-e984-57d1-8558-2dee685815ef" 17592186430260 "answer-10847312-dde2-55cc-bbce-32b3f2b8723c" 17592186430261 "answer-112c77b9-4e4a-5aa1-98f4-ea988ca16426" 17592186430262 "answer-11a82eac-0835-5adf-a299-eda8eba5e6bf" 17592186430263 "answer-15dcf2d0-a1ce-5d9f-971d-640aac12ecec" 17592186430264 "answer-194da90f-9d53-57ff-b9ff-426c6c766b9a" 17592186430265 "answer-2248db21-760b-5d89-a87a-6804c865097b" 1